1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:38,496
What I want to know is, what exactly
did you see during that street fight?

2
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:41,374
That one? Here's what happened.

3
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:43,668
<i>I excused myself to use the restroom.</i>

4
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:44,961
Go stay there.

5
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:46,755
<i>But when I came back out,</i>

6
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>they were all lying on the ground.</i>

7
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:55,513
Once you can picture yourself
wearing that gown on your wedding day,

8
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:58,975
that's how you'll know
it's the right dress.

9
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:07,233
Girls, please take note
of all the adjustments.

10
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>Hey, come on.</i>

11
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:11,905
We've brought the favor you asked for.

12
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,502
You've got a point, Jake.

13
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,879
Of course, I never make half-baked plans.

14
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:29,881
<i>We still have Chiara Valtrovi.</i>

15
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:33,092
She's the one who defeated
La Morte Bianca.

16
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:37,514
That's why she's a legend
no one can surpass.

17
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:41,476
Wait a second.

18
00:01:42,101 --> 00:01:44,020
Do you happen to know…

19
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:46,481
Haven't they ever danced together before?

20
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:51,236
From a distance,
it looks like choreography,

21
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:54,322
but it's definitely not a couple's dance.

22
00:01:59,452 --> 00:02:00,787
Mikoy!

23
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:18,096
Back at the safehouse,
they shared a lot of sweet moments too.

24
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:20,807
There was even CCTV footage
of them slow dancing.

25
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:36,156
That's right. They slow-danced before.

26
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,536
But it's different.

27
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:45,415
Slow dancing when it's just
the two of you, with no one watching,

28
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:48,376
is completely different

29
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:50,378
from being a couple

30
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:53,339
dancing in front of all your guests.

31
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:58,094
And of course, the expectations
are completely different too,

32
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:01,306
when it's your first dance
as husband and wife.

33
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:04,684
I see. So you're saying

34
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:06,728
they're struggling because
of performance anxiety?

35
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:08,688
Is that why
their first dance isn't working?

36
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:12,567
If that's what you call it,

37
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:13,526
then probably, yes.

38
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:19,073
Well, if that's the case,
there's only one solution.

39
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:27,081
Practice until the nerves

40
00:03:27,165 --> 00:03:28,958
and the pressure disappear.

41
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:32,837
Practice until you've overcome
your performance anxiety.

42
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:36,424
Practice until Mikoy and Chiara

43
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,051
can truly enjoy that special moment.

44
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:43,056
We're on the same page!

45
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:45,016
We totally agree with you.

46
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:48,728
I promise Chiara and I will
practice really hard for our

47
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:51,105
very special first dance.

48
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:52,232
- Right, sweetheart?
- Yes.

49
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:53,566
Let's see.

50
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:56,611
- Sorry.
- There you go.

51
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:57,737
- Hey!
- Sorry, sorry!

52
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:00,990
Looks like we need to start
praying a novena

53
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,283
for those two.

54
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:04,661
- Looks like it.
- Sorry, sorry!

55
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:05,411
One more time.

56
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:07,622
They're hurting each other now.

57
00:04:15,546 --> 00:04:16,631
So cute!

58
00:04:24,597 --> 00:04:26,975
Now that your cravings
have been satisfied,

59
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:30,103
and we've brought you
the flavor you wanted…

60
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:37,485
Let's get back to the favor
we're asking from you.

61
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:41,906
What do we need to know

62
00:04:42,573 --> 00:04:44,701
about Senator Quintin?

63
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:05,221
This report is pretty thick.

64
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:30,455
He's close

65
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:32,498
with the generals,

66
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:38,337
They're his neighbors, classmates,

67
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:41,174
even his neighbors in Forbes.

68
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:59,942
Senator Quintin is always winning.

69
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:15,416
But I was wrong.

70
00:06:25,426 --> 00:06:29,931
How can we be sure it's really Quintin?

71
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:32,058
I mean,

72
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:34,477
there are plenty of senators, right?

73
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:56,666
Hello, hello? There!

74
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:58,084
Can you hear me now?

75
00:06:58,167 --> 00:06:59,252
- Yes.
- Okay.

76
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:01,170
Let's gather around. Come over here.

77
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:03,631
Let's get started!

78
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:04,841
All right!

79
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:06,801
Is everyone ready?

80
00:07:09,303 --> 00:07:12,432
Good. It's finally time to begin.

81
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:15,935
The trio you can count on
anytime, anywhere.

82
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:19,355
The trio that can do anything,

83
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:21,023
even dance!

84
00:07:21,107 --> 00:07:22,775
So without further ado,

85
00:07:22,859 --> 00:07:25,194
let's welcome our trio.

86
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:30,116
Captain Pepe, Dekyo, and Jan-Jan!

87
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:46,299
So much effort!

88
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:54,390
A round of applause!

89
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,309
Not bad at all!

90
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:58,644
Looks like someone's not to be outdone.

91
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:01,355
Is it true that this hardworking vlogger

92
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:03,608
is also an amazing performer?

93
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:07,904
Is it true he's become such
a great dancer that he has no more haters?

94
00:08:07,987 --> 00:08:09,363
Well now!

95
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:11,741
Is that true, Rahmboy?

96
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:14,577
Come on, let's prove it!

97
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:18,164
- One, two, three, hey!
- Go, Rahmboy!

98
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:30,593
Good job. Go, Rahmboy!

99
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:34,847
Whoa, that was awesome!

100
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:36,307
Wow!

101
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:38,184
But wait, there's more.

102
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:40,645
They may seem ordinary to you,

103
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:43,314
but don't ever underestimate them.

104
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:45,191
Through everything they've been through,

105
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:47,193
they've stuck together
through thick and thin.

106
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,237
So when it comes to the dance floor,

107
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,405
they won't disappoint!

108
00:08:55,451 --> 00:08:57,870
Our dancing love team!

109
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:03,167
Right.

110
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:04,544
You'd never guess their age!

111
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,255
It's true, love really keeps you young!

112
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:09,632
Of course. That's what happens
when you're perfect for each other.

113
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:13,719
Even when they dance, they move as one.

114
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:16,097
Tess sure knows how to groove!

115
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:17,807
- They're so sweet, right?
- And so is Mario.

116
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:32,405
- I got carried away.
- They're getting better and better.

117
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:34,532
No pressure, though.

118
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:37,076
All right, here's the moment
we've all been waiting for.

119
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,703
Here they come!

120
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:40,037
The couple

121
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:42,790
whose story began in Prague.

122
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:47,420
Fate has tested them time and again.

123
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:51,132
So how will they fare on the dance floor?

124
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,143
Let's go, Mikoy!

125
00:10:02,226 --> 00:10:03,311
- Yes!
- Go, bro! Go!

126
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:07,231
We can do just as well as Mom and Dad.

127
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:09,233
We just have to trust each other.

128
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:10,401
Absolutely.

129
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:14,238
We've been through so much together.
This is just a dance floor.

130
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:15,323
Exactly.

131
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:23,956
- Come on!
- Sorry, sweetheart!

132
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:28,002
That's what I've been telling you.

133
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:38,679
Was it?

134
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:40,890
Because both your feet are left feet.

135
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:44,310
- Mine?
- Both of yours are right feet.

136
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:45,394
Yes.

137
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:48,898
Wait, so how do we do it?

138
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:54,528
No thanks. My feet still hurt
from you stepping on them.

139
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:57,948
Chiara.

140
00:10:58,616 --> 00:10:59,617
- Mikoy.
- What happened?

141
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,826
Come on.

142
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:03,204
- Let's just share.
- That's fine.

143
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:05,915
I thought it was right, left, right, left.

144
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:08,292
Cheating is never easy.

145
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:11,337
I mean, you kept going left.

146
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:15,883
Where did you even see
the left foot go first?

147
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:22,765
Like that.

148
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:25,226
- Sofie.
- Angelito.

149
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:28,062
What happened?

150
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:30,815
How did it come to this?

151
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:35,861
So that woman already told on me.

152
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:38,322
That was fast!

153
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:39,990
She really gets on my nerves!

154
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,077
Sofie, hold on. Calm down first.

155
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:46,789
I just want to know what really happened.

156
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:48,874
Why did you hurt Luisa Mae?

157
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:50,209
Wow.

158
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:53,129
So I'm the only one who got physical?

159
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:54,130
And I wasn't hurt?

160
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:57,800
Me? Why are you assuming,

161
00:11:57,883 --> 00:12:00,761
like you're so sure that I started it?

162
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:07,476
You two got into a fight,

163
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,646
and I just want to know
what really happened.

164
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:12,231
That's why I'm talking to you.

165
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:15,234
You're my friend, Sofie. I know you.

166
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:17,778
You wouldn't just hurt someone
for no reason.

167
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:20,239
But…

168
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,784
I don't think Luisa Mae deserved that.

169
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,327
I feel bad for her.

170
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,163
You feel bad?

171
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:31,417
She deserved it.
And you know what, Angelito?

172
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:34,920
You're being so unfair.

173
00:12:37,506 --> 00:12:39,049
You're my friend.

174
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:42,386
That's why I'm giving you
a chance to explain.

175
00:12:44,388 --> 00:12:47,558
I'm just frustrated that you did that.

176
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:49,977
Well, you know what's frustrating?

177
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:52,980
You're talking to me just to judge me.

178
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:56,108
I thought you were here
to know what really happened.

179
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:58,903
But it turns out you already had
a fixed assumption,

180
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:02,031
and now all you want
is for me to validate it. Right?

181
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:08,120
- Then go be with her!
- There.

182
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:10,581
That's who you are.

183
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:12,583
You just can't let things go.

184
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,295
All I asked was for you
to swallow your pride a little.

185
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:17,755
Just a little.

186
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:19,715
Maybe you're right.

187
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:21,967
Maybe I shouldn't have given you
the benefit of the doubt.

188
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,719
All I ever get from you

189
00:13:23,802 --> 00:13:26,263
are sarcastic answers.

190
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:28,307
I thought you were my friend.

191
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:31,352
I thought you'd always stand
for what's right and good.

192
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:33,896
I guess I was wrong.

193
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:38,692
I made a mistake.

194
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:56,961
Carlota, want some coffee?

195
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:58,546
No, I'm good.

196
00:13:58,629 --> 00:13:59,797
All right, then.

197
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:17,523
You've been awfully quiet.

198
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:21,402
Looks like you're thinking about

199
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:24,196
eating pancit canton too!

200
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:26,115
No.

201
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:30,578
I'm still thinking about
what Viktor told us.

202
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:43,716
Word is,

203
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:45,134
he's sick.

204
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,760
Sick? Terminally ill?

205
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:48,137
Is he dying?

206
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,900
So Senator Quintin really is sick?

207
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:05,863
For now,

208
00:15:06,488 --> 00:15:08,073
we need to find out.

209
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:09,658
Hold on.

210
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:12,119
That's exactly what I'm thinking through.

211
00:15:12,828 --> 00:15:15,205
What should we do with that information?

212
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:18,375
Well, protocol-wise,

213
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:21,086
that's the kind of information

214
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:23,172
we're supposed to report immediately.

215
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:27,051
We should inform
our boss right away, right?

216
00:15:27,801 --> 00:15:31,263
Knowing that Senator Quintin
is a known ally of the agency,

217
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:34,558
we can't just make a move

218
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:35,976
and investigate him.

219
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:37,853
Exactly!

220
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:40,105
And one more thing.

221
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:44,401
Take note that Senator Quintin
is General Norberto's friend.

222
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:46,654
Which means

223
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:50,866
we need to be absolutely sure
of our information before reporting it.

224
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:57,456
this is exactly the kind of information

225
00:15:57,539 --> 00:16:00,668
that could get us burned
if Viktor was wrong.

226
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:05,839
But admit it.

227
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:09,093
This is the tricky part.

228
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:12,554
The part that makes it exciting.

229
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:14,014
The kind where

230
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:17,017
every encounter keeps you on edge!

231
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:18,352
Oh, Cocoy!

232
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:20,104
But seriously,

233
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:24,233
we were recruited into this agency

234
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:27,903
because we each have our own skills.

235
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,613
We're considered assets,

236
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:31,740
and not just assets, but ones

237
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:35,035
who can make a real impact on the team.

238
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:38,914
So what's on your mind?

239
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,931
Let's tail Senator Quintin.

240
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:04,356
Viktor Valtrovi.

241
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,275
Sharing is caring, right?

242
00:17:06,358 --> 00:17:08,402
You've got two boxes.

243
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:12,239
You know the blessings you receive

244
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:14,908
are meant to be shared.

245
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:16,618
So you'll receive even more.

246
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:19,788
That does sound familiar.

247
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,081
Exactly!

248
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:23,042
Since you're easy to talk to,

249
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:27,296
we'll just take one box
of Chilimansi Pancit Canton.

250
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:29,757
You have two anyway.

251
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,884
And since we're in this remote safehouse,

252
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:36,096
we've been craving
Chilimansi Pancit Canton for ages.

253
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:41,351
These are all mine.

254
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:46,732
Cocoy and Carlota.

255
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:48,692
You're turning us down?

256
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:51,195
As if we haven't
been through a lot together.

257
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:54,615
Even I haven't gotten a taste, bosses.

258
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:58,869
Even though Sir Viktor knows
it's my ultimate favorite flavor.

259
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:00,829
Did you hear that?

260
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:10,547
How much less with people
I'm not even close to?

261
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:12,466
Still being stubborn, huh?

262
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:17,429
Then you'll be the one saying sorry.

263
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:19,306
Wait, wait.

264
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,934
What are you doing?

265
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:26,563
All because of Pancit Canton?

266
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,024
Bosses, please.

267
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:34,947
Sir Vik, remember?

268
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:41,578
Come on, just give them a little bit.

269
00:18:42,871 --> 00:18:43,914
You know, Brusko.

270
00:18:50,629 --> 00:18:51,922
Come with me.

271
00:18:52,005 --> 00:18:53,590
- Just relax, Chief.
- Don’t fight.

272
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:56,927
Sir Vik, it's just Pancit Canton.

273
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:19,366
You're the one who totally transformed me!

274
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:23,120
Your injections worked wonders, Doc!

275
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:26,039
But I heard

276
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:28,000
you've raised your rates.

277
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:32,379
It's so hard to book
an appointment with you now.

278
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:49,980
I really didn't mean
to keep stepping on your foot.

279
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:52,816
You know I hate seeing
my sweetheart in pain,

280
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:56,403
especially your cute little feet
that you never let me see,

281
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,322
but now I finally can.

282
00:19:58,405 --> 00:19:59,239
Ouch!

283
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:01,200
Just kidding. I'm sorry.

284
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:04,119
It's okay.

285
00:20:05,287 --> 00:20:07,664
I know you didn't mean it.

286
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:10,667
And I'm sorry too because

287
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:14,713
maybe I was a little too hard on you
during practice earlier,

288
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:17,299
and I snapped at you in front of everyone.

289
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:20,886
It's okay, sweetheart.

290
00:20:20,969 --> 00:20:23,055
Of course I understand.

291
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:25,557
And besides, you're right.

292
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:28,060
It's really hard to dance
when you're injured.

293
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:31,396
It's just strange, sweetheart.

294
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,941
Because if you think about it,
I'm not really stiff.

295
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:38,070
I can groove and shake it whenever I want.

296
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:39,780
And besides,

297
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:42,699
you even fell for me
because of my dance moves.

298
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:44,284
Right?

299
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:47,579
But I don't know.

300
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:50,916
When it comes to couple dancing,
it's like…

301
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:54,711
I completely lose my confidence.

302
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:06,098
I think we're both
just feeling the pressure.

303
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:08,892
Me too.

304
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:12,688
Of course, since this is our first dance

305
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:23,991
It just makes me sad.

306
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:27,786
What if we're really not meant
to be just because we can't

307
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:29,579
dance in sync?

308
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:31,915
What if that's true?

309
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,417
What if I can't do it?

310
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:35,127
What about our wedding?

311
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:36,586
Don't worry, sweetheart.

312
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:39,506
Don't believe that.
It's just superstition.

313
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:41,633
Besides, it's not that important.

314
00:21:41,717 --> 00:21:45,721
Honestly, we could even skip
the first dance as husband and wife.

315
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,389
Yes.

316
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:48,890
What if instead…

317
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:50,017
I know!

318
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:52,185
What if we do our first duet instead?

319
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:53,979
There! That could work.

320
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:57,024
Sweetheart, we're even worse at singing.

321
00:21:59,735 --> 00:22:01,528
Right, right. Good point.

322
00:22:02,904 --> 00:22:04,364
And come on.

323
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:07,909
The first dance is a tradition.

324
00:22:14,791 --> 00:22:16,209
Then…

325
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:19,963
let's just dance.

326
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:23,300
It's okay if it's not perfect.

327
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:36,980
I know we want our first dance
to be something special.

328
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,066
But…

329
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:42,944
maybe it's better if we focus
on the second dance.

330
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:45,238
Or the third.

331
00:22:45,322 --> 00:22:48,200
Or the fifth. Or even the tenth.

332
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:50,911
Or even our hundredth, sweetheart.

333
00:22:52,370 --> 00:22:55,123
Because isn't what really matters

334
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:57,084
that no matter what song life plays,

335
00:22:58,543 --> 00:23:00,295
we'll always dance through it together?

336
00:23:02,714 --> 00:23:04,466
Isn't that what truly matters?

337
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:30,784
Wait, sweetheart.

338
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:33,120
Are you sure?

339
00:23:33,203 --> 00:23:34,412
What if

340
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:36,665
I step on your foot again?

341
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:38,917
Come on.

342
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,919
If I can handle taking punches,

343
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:43,713
I'm sure I can handle
you stepping on my foot.

344
00:23:44,631 --> 00:23:48,677
Besides, I'm dancing
with the person I love most.

345
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,972
- Come on.
- All right, then.

346
00:25:47,295 --> 00:25:49,172
- He’s my patient.
- What’s his diagnostic?

347
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:50,840
I can’t tell you that.

348
00:25:50,924 --> 00:25:52,300
And why is that?!

349
00:25:55,178 --> 00:25:57,722
Do you not know what we can do to you?

350
00:25:57,806 --> 00:26:00,934
I can’t destroy my oath as a doctor.

351
00:26:01,017 --> 00:26:04,062
Even if you tied me up or kill me.

352
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:07,649
Chiara, take a look at this.

353
00:26:07,732 --> 00:26:09,234
Is this you?

354
00:26:09,317 --> 00:26:10,652
Oh, no.

355
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:11,778
Are you sure?

356
00:26:12,362 --> 00:26:14,656
It really isn’t me. Believe me.

357
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:16,616
If that’s not you,

358
00:26:18,159 --> 00:26:19,327
who’s that?

359
00:26:23,206 --> 00:26:24,666
There’s someone who wants to meet you.

360
00:26:24,749 --> 00:26:27,335
- Who?
- A new person with lots of connections.

361
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:30,338
All the favors Viktor,
he can give it to you.

362
00:26:34,801 --> 00:26:36,469
I’m starting to get nervous.

363
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:38,138
Why? What’s your theory?

364
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:40,724
La Morte Bianca is gone.

365
00:26:40,807 --> 00:26:42,434
But not the Concordat.

366
00:26:42,517 --> 00:26:43,977
Alex.

367
00:26:44,060 --> 00:26:45,228
I want to get married.

368
00:26:45,312 --> 00:26:47,314
Start a new normal life.

369
00:26:47,397 --> 00:26:49,149
I don’t want it to get ruined.
